# Ad-hoc deploy package, rebuilt on demand — not source
market-workflow-deploy.zip

# server/public is INTENTIONALLY tracked (not ignored), despite being a
# build artifact: vercel.json ships it to the Vercel function via
# `includeFiles`, and Vercel's build step never rebuilds the client itself
# in this project's config — so the committed copy IS what gets deployed.
# Run `npm run build:vercel` to refresh it before committing/pushing any
# client change. (It's also reused, and overwritten, by `npm run build:exe`
# — that's fine, both just want the latest client build there.)

# Created locally by `vercel link` / `vercel dev`
.vercel/
